"The phenomenological experience of suffering, the subjective reality of pain and despair, can be so overwhelming that it eclipses all other considerations.",1
"The individual may experience a profound sense of anhedonia, the inability to experience pleasure or joy, further reinforcing the perception of a life devoid of meaning.",1
"The teleological question of purpose, the search for a reason to continue living, becomes paramount in the face of such profound distress.",1
